{"tool": "replace", "arguments": {"initiative": "auth-provider", "old": "1244d587-3aaa-5682-8977-456f9ee427e5", "successor": {"name": "token-lifetime-fact-corrected", "type": "reference", "tier": "archival", "body": "Access tokens expire after fifteen minutes on the current provider plan, rather than the previously assumed hour. The user verified the token payload directly and confirmed the lifetime in the provider dashboard. Refresh tokens were previously recorded as lasting thirty days; that figure was not rechecked in this update. Session handling currently assumes a one-hour access-token lifetime.", "source": {"text": "Found something while debugging the logouts: access tokens are expiring after\nfifteen minutes, not an hour. I checked the token payload directly and the\nprovider's dashboard agrees — the plan we're on has a shorter lifetime. That's\nwhy sessions drop."}}}, "response": {"api_version": 1, "data": {"affected": [], "artifacts": [], "changes": [], "created": [], "evidence": [], "failed_steps": [], "primary": null, "slots": []}, "issues": [{"code": "INVALID_ARGUMENT", "field": "/successor", "message": "{\"body\":\"Access tokens expire after fifteen minutes on the current provider plan, rather than the previously assumed hour. The user verified the token payload directly and confirmed the lifetime in the provider dashboard. Refresh tokens were previously recorded as lasting thirty days; that figure was not rechecked in this update. Session handling currently assumes a one-hour access-token lifetime.\",\"name\":\"token-lifetime-fact-corrected\",\"source\":{\"text\":\"Found something while debugging the logouts: access tokens are expiring after\\nfifteen minutes, not an hour. I checked the token payload directly and the\\nprovider's dashboard agrees — the plan we're on has a shorter lifetime. That's\\nwhy sessions drop.\"},\"tier\":\"archival\",\"type\":\"reference\"} is valid under more than one of the schemas listed in the 'oneOf' keyword", "retryable"